  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Terrapin Station** (1 review): Comes A Time into Throwing Stones into Terrapin closed the first set and was a highlight for the reviewer [3]\n- **Playing in the Band** (1 review): Reviewer especially enjoyed the Playing in the Band, Uncle John's Band, Playing in the Band sequence in the strong second set [3]\n- **Touch of Grey** (1 review): Reviewer found the encore lacking; the slower tempo didn't suit a song that should rock hard [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **A Hard Rain's A-Gonna Fall**: rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **DeadCo2019-06-08.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 182 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the recording sounds great, with almost no audible crowd noise [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The taper recorded from Section 102, Row 18 [1]\n- Reviewer notes Meyer plays a lot of notes during the show [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **DeadCo2019-06-08.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64v's>VMS5u>Sound Devices 744t [1]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps CMC64V microphones through a Schoeps VMS5u preamp into a Sound Devices 744t recorder; Post-production: Soundforge Pro 11 for fades and levels, CDWAV track splitting, Trader's Little Helper for FLAC, Foobar2000 for tagging [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Gorge Amphitheatre: [Dead & Company Tickets | 8 June 2019 | Gorge Amphitheatre](https://www.georgeamphitheatre.com/events/dead-company-3/) [5]",
